  'implied' is sqrt(var(actual) - mean within-start var): how
  much start-to-start variation really exists. 'our spread' is
  the sd of our per-start predicted means, 'share' the ratio.
  'ceiling' is the correlation a PERFECT forecaster would get
  (implied/actual sd); 'of ceil' is how much of it we capture.

